      "notes": "Montages, captions and native complete diagrams reviewed. Begin at the complete sixteen-piece diagram after Kf4 36 seconds: White Kf4/Qc8/Rf8/Bd3/d4/e3/g3/h4 against Kh6/Qg6/Bg4/d7/e6/f6/g7/h5. Native13 establishes the full reversed board. The offered queen goes to e4, despite caption d4. Both legal White replies to Qe4+ are covered: Bxe4 and Kxe4. After the pawn-check sequence, g5+ is not immediate mate: White must answer hxg5+, then fxg5# is actual mate. Native27/28/29 show that complete bishop-capture finish, including the white pawn on g5 and then Black f6xg5. Native34/35 illustrate the corresponding king-capture branch. The prior legal-only review stopped before the final recapture; it is preserved and corrected rather than silently discarded. A complete finite Black strategy checks every White reply through actual mate, with all sixteen root pieces retained. Earlier queen/bishop-capture blunders and king-escape alternatives before this root remain outside the proof.",
